{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-415a1167-f8b8-4907-9f26-71a01fc05ab6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a5f2d1f64678319d","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-z19ov__w/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E001.md","content":"# Confirm PQC base image availability and timing (python/nodejs variants, RHEL 9.8 rebase)\n\n## Description\n\nThis investigation resolves the strategy's gating unknowns around PQC base image supply: whether PQC-enabled variants of the `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22` base images will exist by the September 15, 2026 compliance deadline, and the committed date for the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase that gates `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` adoption. Both questions are tracked through the AIPCC team's spike (RHOAIENG-7195, with AIPCC-7258 for the rebase). The outcome determines the remediation path — base image switch versus OCP exception filing — for the roughly ten python/nodejs-based RHOAI images and the adoption timing for the roughly thirty-four rhel9-els-based images.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Engage the AIPCC team to obtain, for each of `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22`: a committed availability date for a PQC-enabled variant, or a confirmed statement that no variant will be available by September 15, 2026\n- Obtain the committed date for the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258) that gates adoption of `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`\n- Escalate per the strategy's risk mitigation if no committed date is obtained by early September\n- Publish the confirmed availability and timing outcomes so per-image remediation paths (switch vs. OCP exception) can be finalized in the PQC readiness matrix and compliance tracking\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given the AIPCC spike tracking PQC base image variants, when this investigation completes, then each of the four base image families has a confirmed status: PQC variant available by September 15, 2026; available only at a stated later date; or confirmed unavailable\n- The AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase has a committed date or a confirmed slip, with the impact on `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` adoption recorded\n- Escalation is triggered if no committed date is obtained by early September, per the strategy's stated mitigation\n- Results are recorded in a form consumable by the PQC readiness matrix and the compliance tracking effort\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image** — partial: determines which image groups can take the switch path\n- **[P0] Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception** — partial: identifies the image groups that are likely exception candidates if variants or the rebase are not available in time\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":46351,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c2678e3b0c94713","agent_id":"a5b92c748e1d652f4","session_id":"44116bc5-5d92-4984-8d6b-f35b618127c9","uuid":"87e67653-565e-4fd3-80a1-08df8b7921cd","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:54:34.145Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001 into epics"}
