{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-3d11c7cb-51ee-4b01-bb63-e9afe3513b6a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9623e9484fdc05d0","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-z19ov__w/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E002.md","content":"# PQC compliance tracking and aggregation for RHOAI runtime images\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the strategy's core coordination work: an aggregated, deadline-enforced compliance view across every RHOAI runtime image for the September 15, 2026 cutoff. Component teams own their base image switches and exception filings; this epic ensures none of that work goes unaccounted for — tracking tickets are linked for OCP 5.0 visibility, teams are reminded on a weekly cadence, the OCP exception process is exercised for teams that cannot comply, and leadership escalation fires for teams at risk of missing the deadline without coverage.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Establish and maintain tracking tickets from every RHOAI component team linked to the strategy, providing the aggregated compliance view for OCP 5.0\n- Reconcile the full image inventory (the RHOAI 3.5 bundle CSV's 153 relatedImages) against per-image status — switched to a PQC base, exception filed, or pending — so that zero images remain unaccounted for at the deadline\n- Run weekly reminders to component teams; escalate to leadership per the Mara/Devin sync decision for teams at risk of missing September 15 without an exception filed\n- Track OCP exception filings via the OCPEXCEPT process and confirm each filing documents the component's TLS stack and the reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM, with a remediation plan\n- Identify teams using non-OpenSSL TLS stacks (rustls+ring, Java/NSS) — fms-guardrails-orchestrator, TrustyAI explainability, trainer data cache — and confirm each has either an exception filing or an alternate remediation in progress\n- Communicate the runtime-only constraint to all teams: only the final stage of the Dockerfile/Containerfile changes; no builder image change is needed\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- All component team tracking tickets are linked to the strategy, providing an aggregated compliance view for OCP 5.0 (strategy AC-3)\n- By September 15, 2026, every RHOAI component image has either (a) been rebuilt on a PQC-enabled base image, or (b) a filed and acknowledged OCP exception in OCPEXCEPT with a documented remediation plan including the component's TLS stack and reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM — zero unaccounted-for images remain (strategy AC-2)\n- Weekly reminder cadence is demonstrably executed through the deadline window, with escalations raised for non-responding or at-risk teams\n- Every image in the RHOAI 3.5/3.6 payload inventory is reconciled to a switch, an exception, or a tracked pending state at all times\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image** — drives and aggregates the per-team switch work\n- **[P0] Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception** — enforces the exception process and deadline\n- **[P0] PQC enablement is runtime only** — communicates the final-stage-only constraint to teams\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":47228,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c2678e3b0c94713","agent_id":"a5b92c748e1d652f4","session_id":"44116bc5-5d92-4984-8d6b-f35b618127c9","uuid":"7c7dba67-5c79-4b87-ac25-76c9b8f87611","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:54:48.762Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001 into epics"}
