ndidates with their TLS stack and reason documented\n- Reflect the confirmed availability outcomes for python/nodejs PQC variants and the RHEL 9.8 rebase timing in the final remediation paths\n- Document that remediation is runtime-only — only the final stage of each Dockerfile/Containerfile changes, no builder image change\n- Note deferred items (ML-DSA / PQC-signed X.509 certificates) as explicitly out of scope\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Every image in the RHOAI 3.5/3.6 payload inventory appears exactly once in the matrix with all fields populated or explicitly marked as exception-path\n- TLS stack classifications are consistent with the platform architecture context (e.g., fms-guardrails-orchestrator uses rustls+ring and cannot inherit PQC from a base image; TrustyAI uses Java/NSS)\n- The remediation path for python/nodejs-based and rhel9-els-based images reflects the confirmed availability and timing outcomes for those base images\n- Every switch-path entry specifies the final runtime stage as the only changed element, per the runtime-only constraint\n- The matrix is technically reviewed for accuracy against the architecture context and the confirmed base image availability\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image** — defines the per-image target base and path\n- **[P0] Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception** — identifies exception-path images with TLS stack and reason\n- **[P0] PQC enablement is runtime only** — documents the final-stage-only constraint per image\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":48062,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c2678e3b0c94713","agent_id":"a5b92c748e1d652f4","session_id":"44116bc5-5d92-4984-8d6b-f35b618127c9","uuid":"10283449-deed-4313-878d-b30f6a3f1c64","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:55:02.437Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"De