{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-00306662-0e37-4ad9-99f7-82f035fb5cff","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-afb2684db6096cfa","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-z19ov__w/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-E004.md","content":"# Automated PQC compliance verification scan across the RHOAI payload\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the automated CI scan that measures the strategy's primary acceptance criterion: for every RHOAI runtime image in the 3.6 payload, verify inside the container that the active crypto policy is `DEFAULT:PQ` and that ML-KEM algorithms are available from the system OpenSSL. It produces the per-image compliance report used for the aggregated OCP 5.0 compliance view, distinguishing OpenSSL-backed components (which must pass) from non-OpenSSL components covered by OCP exception filings.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Build an automated scan that, for each image in the RHOAI 3.6 payload, executes the equivalent of `update-crypto-policies --show` and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` inside the container and records the results\n- Expected pass state for OpenSSL-backed components: active crypto policy `DEFAULT:PQ`, and ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024 present in the kem-algorithms output\n- Classify each image as pass, fail, or exception-covered, using the readiness matrix's TLS stack classification so non-OpenSSL components (rustls+ring, Java/NSS) are reported as exception-covered rather than failed\n- Handle the FIPS-mode carve-out: on FIPS-mode clusters, FIPS policy deactivates PQC for this release — this is expected behavior per the strategy's confirmed assumptions and must not be reported as a compliance failure\n- Produce a per-image report consumable by the compliance tracking effort across the full payload\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The scan runs in CI across the RHOAI 3.6 payload without manual per-image setup\n- For OpenSSL-backed images, the scan verifies active policy `DEFAULT:PQ` and presence of ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024 (strategy AC-1 measurement)\n- Non-OpenSSL components are reported as exception-covered, not failed\n- FIPS-mode cluster behavior is classified as expected/non-compliant-free per the strategy note\n- A per-image compliance report is produced for the aggregated compliance view\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image** — verification and measurement of the outcome\n- **[P0] PQC enablement is runtime only** — verifies the runtime crypto policy inside containers, not the builder stage\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":48980,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c2678e3b0c94713","agent_id":"a5b92c748e1d652f4","session_id":"44116bc5-5d92-4984-8d6b-f35b618127c9","uuid":"c013dd01-b85b-4d90-a7bc-f171e7ea76fe","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:55:12.538Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001 into epics"}
