reed threshold before ship\n- Non-PQC clients are demonstrably able to connect via classic ECDHE (backwards compatibility per the IETF hybrid key exchange draft)\n- No change in HA characteristics is observed relative to the pre-PQC payload\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- No HLR maps directly to this epic; it covers the strategy's Non-Functional Requirements: Performance (regression threshold and measurement), Backwards compatibility, and Availability\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":49682,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9c2678e3b0c94713","agent_id":"a5b92c748e1d652f4","session_id":"44116bc5-5d92-4984-8d6b-f35b618127c9","uuid":"c2116f1d-ea9c-41a8-ae20-382ab52ab2f4","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:55:21.368Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001 into epics"}
