{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-85315f0b01fa3fff","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n3\ttitle: Confirm PQC base image availability and timing (python/nodejs variants, RHEL\n4\t  9.8 rebase)\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n6\tcomponent: AIPCC Ecosystems\n7\tteam: AIPCC team\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Low\n20\tai_implementability_score: -1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Confirm PQC base image availability and timing (python/nodejs variants, RHEL 9.8 rebase)\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's gating unknowns around PQC base image supply: whether PQC-enabled variants of the `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22` base images will exist by the September 15, 2026 compliance deadline, and the committed date for the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase that gates `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` adoption. Both questions are tracked through the AIPCC team's spike (RHOAIENG-7195, with AIPCC-7258 for the rebase). The outcome determines the remediation path — base image switch versus OCP exception filing — for the roughly ten python/nodejs-based RHOAI images and the adoption timing for the roughly thirty-four rhel9-els-based images.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Engage the AIPCC team to obtain, for each of `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/python-312-minimal`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22`: a committed availability date for a PQC-enabled variant, or a confirmed statement that no variant will be available by September 15, 2026\n35\t- Obtain the committed date for the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258) that gates adoption of `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`\n36\t- Escalate per the strategy's risk mitigation if no committed date is obtained by early September\n37\t- Publish the confirmed availability and timing outcomes so per-image remediation paths (switch vs. OCP exception) can be finalized in the PQC readiness matrix and compliance tracking\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- Given the AIPCC spike tracking PQC base image variants, when this investigation completes, then each of the four base image families has a confirmed status: PQC variant available by September 15, 2026; available only at a stated later date; or confirmed unavailable\n42\t- The AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase has a committed date or a confirmed slip, with the impact on `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` adoption recorded\n43\t- Escalation is triggered if no committed date is obtained by early September, per the strategy's stated mitigation\n44\t- Results are recorded in a form consumable by the PQC readiness matrix and the compliance tracking effort\n45\t\n46\t## HLR Traceability\n47\t\n48\t- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image** — partial: determines which image groups can take the switch path\n49\t- **[P0] Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception** — partial: identifies the image groups that are likely exception candidates if variants or the rebase are not available in time\n50\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ceb8fab52b3cedf","agent_id":"aae5a817836ac1f40","session_id":"44116bc5-5d92-4984-8d6b-f35b618127c9","uuid":"62819c88-1743-4c4a-9f8b-f55de430f408","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:57:53.015Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-85315f0b01fa3fff","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
