{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfb75649a12a798d","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E004\n3\ttitle: Automated PQC compliance verification scan across the RHOAI payload\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: CI/CD\n6\tteam: DevOps/Build team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Automated PQC compliance verification scan across the RHOAI payload\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the automated CI scan that measures the strategy's primary acceptance criterion: for every RHOAI runtime image in the 3.6 payload, verify inside the container that the active crypto policy is `DEFAULT:PQ` and that ML-KEM algorithms are available from the system OpenSSL. It produces the per-image compliance report used for the aggregated OCP 5.0 compliance view, distinguishing OpenSSL-backed components (which must pass) from non-OpenSSL components covered by OCP exception filings.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Build an automated scan that, for each image in the RHOAI 3.6 payload, executes the equivalent of `update-crypto-policies --show` and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` inside the container and records the results\n38\t- Expected pass state for OpenSSL-backed components: active crypto policy `DEFAULT:PQ`, and ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024 present in the kem-algorithms output\n39\t- Classify each image as pass, fail, or exception-covered, using the readiness matrix's TLS stack classification so non-OpenSSL components (rustls+ring, Java/NSS) are reported as exception-covered rather than failed\n40\t- Handle the FIPS-mode carve-out: on FIPS-mode clusters, FIPS policy deactivates PQC for this release — this is expected behavior per the strategy's confirmed assumptions and must not be reported as a compliance failure\n41\t- Produce a per-image report consumable by the compliance tracking effort across the full payload\n42\t\n43\t## Acceptance Criteria\n44\t\n45\t- The scan runs in CI across the RHOAI 3.6 payload without manual per-image setup\n46\t- For OpenSSL-backed images, the scan verifies active policy `DEFAULT:PQ` and presence of ML-KEM-512, ML-KEM-768, and ML-KEM-1024 (strategy AC-1 measurement)\n47\t- Non-OpenSSL components are reported as exception-covered, not failed\n48\t- FIPS-mode cluster behavior is classified as expected/non-compliant-free per the strategy note\n49\t- A per-image compliance report is produced for the aggregated compliance view\n50\t\n51\t## HLR Traceability\n52\t\n53\t- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image** — verification and measurement of the outcome\n54\t- **[P0] PQC enablement is runtime only** — verifies the runtime crypto policy inside containers, not the builder stage\n55\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ceb8fab52b3cedf","agent_id":"aae5a817836ac1f40","session_id":"44116bc5-5d92-4984-8d6b-f35b618127c9","uuid":"21e3b82a-d828-4ed8-9068-b184d1f7bc41","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:57:55.295Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfb75649a12a798d","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
