{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfaa70e7f7ecda77","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E005\n3\ttitle: TLS handshake performance regression threshold and measurement\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: PerfScale\n6\tteam: Performance team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: -1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: -1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 0\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: Medium\n23\tai_implementability_score: 1\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# TLS handshake performance regression threshold and measurement\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic resolves the strategy's non-functional requirement marked as needing domain input — the missing numeric TLS handshake regression threshold — and produces the pre-ship measurement of TLS handshake latency regression for the PQC-enabled RHOAI payload. PQC hybrid key exchange (X25519MLKEM768) is negotiated opportunistically, so the measurement must confirm both that handshake latency stays within the agreed threshold and that non-PQC clients continue to work via classic ECDHE without availability or HA changes.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Define the numeric TLS handshake regression threshold with the PM and Performance team lead — the strategy requires this to be resolved before Sprint 2 ends (currently marked \"NEEDS DOMAIN INPUT\"; reference points: Chrome ~10% maximum TLS handshake time regression, and the Red Hat PQC benchmarking outcome PSASTRAT-7170)\n38\t- Measure TLS handshake latency on the rebuilt PQC-enabled RHOAI payload (hybrid X25519MLKEM768 vs. classic ECDHE) and report the regression against the agreed threshold before ship\n39\t- Confirm backwards compatibility: clients that do not support PQC continue to work via classic ECDHE opportunistic negotiation\n40\t- Confirm the base image switch does not change HA characteristics (no additional replicas required)\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- A numeric TLS handshake regression threshold is agreed and documented by the PM and Performance team lead before Sprint 2 ends\n45\t- TLS handshake latency regression is measured on the rebuilt PQC-enabled payload and reported against the agreed threshold before ship\n46\t- Non-PQC clients are demonstrably able to connect via classic ECDHE (backwards compatibility per the IETF hybrid key exchange draft)\n47\t- No change in HA characteristics is observed relative to the pre-PQC payload\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- No HLR maps directly to this epic; it covers the strategy's Non-Functional Requirements: Performance (regression threshold and measurement), Backwards compatibility, and Availability\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8ceb8fab52b3cedf","agent_id":"aae5a817836ac1f40","session_id":"44116bc5-5d92-4984-8d6b-f35b618127c9","uuid":"948f0f0e-a08e-4540-a57c-e19750dc7e6f","timestamp":"2026-10-22T08:57:56.010Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bfaa70e7f7ecda77","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
