{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-81abcef405bbeda8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E003\n3\ttitle: PQC Readiness Matrix per RHOAI component image\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: OpenShift AI Productization\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If PQC variants of the python/nodejs base images or the AIPCC\n15\t    RHEL 9.8 rebase are not confirmed available in time, the affected image groups\n16\t    are marked for the OCP-exception remediation path in the readiness matrix instead\n17\t    of base image switches, and the exception-tracking scope expands accordingly.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 0\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 3\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# PQC Readiness Matrix per RHOAI component image\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tThis epic produces the design document the strategy calls for: a PQC Readiness Matrix covering every RHOAI runtime image, classifying each image's TLS stack, current base image, target PQC base image, remediation path (final-stage base switch vs. OCP exception), owning team, and linked tracking ticket. It is the analysis artifact that tells every component team which of the two compliance paths applies to them and what specifically changes (runtime stage only). It incorporates the confirmed availability and timing outcomes for the python/nodejs PQC base image variants and the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase once known.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Build the readiness matrix from the RHOAI 3.5 image inventory (the bundle CSV's 153 relatedImages) and the organized local image inventory (`3.5-component-images-organized.md`)\n44\t- For each image, record: current base image; target PQC base (`ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`, `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`, or a python/nodejs PQC variant); TLS stack classification (system OpenSSL / rustls+ring / Java NSS); remediation path (final-stage base switch vs. OCP exception); owning team; linked tracking ticket\n45\t- Apply the strategy's base image mapping: ~68 ubi9-minimal images → `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`; ~34 rhel9-els images (notebooks, workbenches, training runtimes, mlserver) → `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`; ~10 python/nodejs-based images → variant-dependent; the TrustyAI Java image → exception expected (NSS backend, not OpenSSL)\n46\t- Mark components that cannot be remediated by a base image swap alone (rustls+ring, Java/NSS) as exception-path candidates with their TLS stack and reason documented\n47\t- Reflect the confirmed availability outcomes for python/nodejs PQC variants and the RHEL 9.8 rebase timing in the final remediation paths\n48\t- Document that remediation is runtime-only — only the final stage of each Dockerfile/Containerfile changes, no builder image change\n49\t- Note deferred items (ML-DSA / PQC-signed X.509 certificates) as explicitly out of scope\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- Every image in the RHOAI 3.5/3.6 payload inventory appears exactly once in the matrix with all fields populated or explicitly marked as exception-path\n54\t- TLS stack classifications are consistent with the platform architecture context (e.g., fms-guardrails-orchestrator uses rustls+ring and cannot inherit PQC from a base image; TrustyAI uses Java/NSS)\n55\t- The remediation path for python/nodejs-based and rhel9-els-based images reflects the confirmed availability and timing outcomes for those base images\n56\t- Every switch-path entry specifies the final runtime stage as the only changed element, per the runtime-only constraint\n57\t- The matrix is technically reviewed for accuracy against the architecture context and the confirmed base image availability\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image** — defines the per-image target base and path\n62\t- **[P0] Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception** — identifies exception-path images with TLS stack and reason\n63\t- **[P0] PQC enablement is runtime only** — documents the final-stage-only constraint per image\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a03658d894d6bd33","agent_id":"adaa49669441be4d2","session_id":"44116bc5-5d92-4984-8d6b-f35b618127c9","uuid":"7c48d8f0-4360-41c5-a689-42efda9a4d6c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:01:12.142Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-81abcef405bbeda8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
