{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b022035837a0315c","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E002\n3\ttitle: PQC compliance tracking and aggregation for RHOAI runtime images\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: OpenShift AI Productization\n6\tteam: OpenShift AI Productization\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: -1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 0\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 3\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# PQC compliance tracking and aggregation for RHOAI runtime images\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic delivers the strategy's core coordination work: an aggregated, deadline-enforced compliance view across every RHOAI runtime image for the September 15, 2026 cutoff. Component teams own their base image switches and exception filings; this epic ensures none of that work goes unaccounted for — tracking tickets are linked for OCP 5.0 visibility, teams are reminded on a weekly cadence, the OCP exception process is exercised for teams that cannot comply, and leadership escalation fires for teams at risk of missing the deadline without coverage.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Establish and maintain tracking tickets from every RHOAI component team linked to the strategy, providing the aggregated compliance view for OCP 5.0\n38\t- Reconcile the full image inventory (the RHOAI 3.5 bundle CSV's 153 relatedImages) against per-image status — switched to a PQC base, exception filed, or pending — so that zero images remain unaccounted for at the deadline\n39\t- Run weekly reminders to component teams; escalate to leadership per the Mara/Devin sync decision for teams at risk of missing September 15 without an exception filed\n40\t- Track OCP exception filings via the OCPEXCEPT process and confirm each filing documents the component's TLS stack and the reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM, with a remediation plan\n41\t- Identify teams using non-OpenSSL TLS stacks (rustls+ring, Java/NSS) — fms-guardrails-orchestrator, TrustyAI explainability, trainer data cache — and confirm each has either an exception filing or an alternate remediation in progress\n42\t- Once the per-image readiness matrix's TLS stack classification is available, cross-check the non-OpenSSL team list against it so the day-one list (drawn from the strategy's named teams) converges with the per-image analysis instead of maintaining duplicate TLS analysis\n43\t- Communicate the runtime-only constraint to all teams: only the final stage of the Dockerfile/Containerfile changes; no builder image change is needed\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance Criteria\n46\t\n47\t- All component team tracking tickets are linked to the strategy, providing an aggregated compliance view for OCP 5.0 (strategy AC-3)\n48\t- By September 15, 2026, every RHOAI component image has either (a) been rebuilt on a PQC-enabled base image, or (b) a filed and acknowledged OCP exception in OCPEXCEPT with a documented remediation plan including the component's TLS stack and reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM — zero unaccounted-for images remain (strategy AC-2)\n49\t- Weekly reminder cadence is demonstrably executed through the deadline window, with escalations raised for non-responding or at-risk teams\n50\t- Every image in the RHOAI 3.5/3.6 payload inventory is reconciled to a switch, an exception, or a tracked pending state at all times\n51\t\n52\t## HLR Traceability\n53\t\n54\t- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image** — drives and aggregates the per-team switch work\n55\t- **[P0] Teams unable to comply by September 15 must file an OCP exception** — enforces the exception process and deadline\n56\t- **[P0] PQC enablement is runtime only** — communicates the final-stage-only constraint to teams\n57\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7a2dad174209422","agent_id":"a78dcda41674ce424","session_id":"44116bc5-5d92-4984-8d6b-f35b618127c9","uuid":"8617f2e7-a44c-45e1-b948-1f5baa936d66","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:03:21.765Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b022035837a0315c","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
