{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7e6ade237f8976f","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E006\n3\ttitle: PQC base image availability in RHOAI build infrastructure\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: Build and Release\n6\tteam: DevOps/Build team\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 0\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 0\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# PQC base image availability in RHOAI build infrastructure\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic makes the confirmed PQC base images consumable by RHOAI component builds and coordinates the shared build pipeline updates, so that component teams can execute their final-stage base switches without pipeline blockers. The two confirmed images — `registry.redhat.io/ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` and `registry.redhat.io/rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`, both reporting `DEFAULT:PQ` — are available upstream (confirmed August 2026, OCPSTRAT-7413); this epic covers their availability to and consumption by the RHOAI build infrastructure.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Make `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` and `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` consumable by the RHOAI build infrastructure, following existing base image pipeline practice\n38\t- Update shared build configuration references (RHOAI-Build-Config) where base images are centrally managed\n39\t- Coordinate base image pipeline updates across component builds and publish guidance for teams switching their final runtime stages\n40\t- Track follow-up availability of the python/nodejs PQC base image variants and make them consumable once their availability is confirmed (follow-up scope, not a blocker for this epic's confirmed-image work)\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- Both confirmed PQC base images are consumable by component builds through the RHOAI build pipeline\n45\t- Shared build configuration no longer references only non-PQC bases where base images are centrally managed\n46\t- Component teams are able to execute final-stage base switches without pipeline blockers, per team feedback through the compliance tracking effort\n47\t- Guidance for the runtime-stage-only switch is published to component teams\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- **[P0] All RHOAI runtime images must use a PQC-enabled base image** — enablement: build infrastructure readiness for the per-team switches\n52\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a7a2dad174209422","agent_id":"a78dcda41674ce424","session_id":"44116bc5-5d92-4984-8d6b-f35b618127c9","uuid":"4129b4c7-a902-42c8-af98-4b739ac7d30b","timestamp":"2026-10-22T09:03:29.841Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7e6ade237f8976f","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
